.TH HEADROOM 1 "2026-10-20" "Headroom 0.1.0-beta.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
headroom \- weekly Claude and Codex allowance left, against the time left until renewal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B headroom
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.br
.B headroom statusline
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR claude | tmux | sketchybar | plain ]
.RB [ \-\-provider
.IR claude | codex ]
.br
.B headroom wait
.RB [ \-\-provider
.IR claude | codex | any ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR duration ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B headroom mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B headroom
prints what Headroom.app knows about your Claude and OpenAI Codex plans: how much of
the weekly allowance is left, how long until it renews, the pacing verdict, the 5-hour
session, model caps and reset credits.
.PP
It reads only the snapshot the app writes to
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Headroom/snapshot.json" .
It never reads credentials and never uses the network. When the app isn't running it
prints the last snapshot and says how old it is.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B headroom
One line per provider (emoji cells, percent left, time to renewal), then indented lines
for the verdict, the 5-hour session, blocks, faults and reset credits. The session line
is a warning from the level set in Settings (75% used by default), an amber heads-up when
the recent pace runs it out before its reset, and a dim line with the spare share otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Every number in the snapshot, plus
.B stale
and
.BR age_seconds .
Schema version 1. Each session carries
.BR outlook " (idle, comfortable, lasts, runs_out, blocked),"
.B runs_out_at
and
.BR left_at_reset .
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Asks the app for fresh limits (a Darwin notification,
.BR com.headroom.refresh ),
then waits up to 10 seconds for a new snapshot. Requests closer than 30 seconds apart
reuse the current snapshot.
.TP
.B statusline
One short line for a prompt, tmux, SketchyBar or Claude Code's status line. It reads and
ignores Claude Code's JSON on standard input. Colors use ANSI (claude) or tmux style
codes (tmux); sketchybar and plain have none.
.B NO_COLOR
turns colors off.
.TP
.B wait
Blocks while the 5-hour session or the weekly limit is at 100%, or a major outage is
active, then returns. It wakes when the snapshot changes or at the reset time and uses
no CPU while waiting. With
.B \-\-provider any
(the default) it returns as soon as either provider has capacity.
.B \-\-json
prints
.B {"blocked_by", "until"}
first.
.TP
.B mcp
Optional. A stdio Model Context Protocol server with one read-only tool,
.BR get_headroom .
Add it with:
.B claude mcp add \-\-scope user headroom \-\- ~/.local/bin/headroom mcp
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for
.BR wait ,
capacity is back.
.TP
.B 2
.B wait
timed out.
.TP
.B 3
No snapshot exists yet (open Headroom.app).
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colors.
.TP
.B HEADROOM_HOME
Reads the snapshot from this directory instead.
.SH FILES
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Headroom/snapshot.json
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
headroom
headroom statusline \-\-format tmux
headroom wait \-\-provider claude && claude \-p "continue the refactor"
.fi
